From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: preserve configuration supplied by distribution Meson

Meson copies its configured Rust constants into the source tree. A subsequent
Cargo build currently configures another Meson build with its default options,
silently replacing distribution paths such as /usr/share and persistent first
boot settings output with /usr/local/share and /run.

Let distribution builds declare that Meson was already configured, retaining
the development fallback and the existing Debian guard. Track the new setting
so a reused Cargo target directory rebuilds when this mode changes.
---
diff --git a/build.rs b/build.rs
--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -8,7 +8,10 @@ fn main() {
         "mobi.phosh.FirstBoot.gresource",
     );
 
-    if env::var("DEB_HOST_ARCH").is_err() {
+    println!("cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=PFB_MESON_PRECONFIGURED");
+    let meson_preconfigured =
+        env::var("PFB_MESON_PRECONFIGURED").is_ok_and(|value| value == "1");
+    if !meson_preconfigured && env::var("DEB_HOST_ARCH").is_err() {
         let meson_dir = format!("{}/_build/", env::var("OUT_DIR").unwrap());
         Command::new("meson")
             .args(["setup", "--reconfigure", &meson_dir])
